    "q-111645": {
      "dom_id": "step-q111645",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Factor the expression $98{s}^{2}+84s+18.$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that all of the terms have a common factor of $2.$ Therefore, we can simplify the expression by factoring out $2,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}98{s}^{2}+84s+18 & = \\\\ 2(49{s}^{2}+42s+9)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's factor the expression inside parentheses using the square of a sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}49{s}^{2}+42s+9 & = \\\\ (7s)^{2}+42s+{3}^{2} & = \\\\ (7s)^{2}+2\\cdot (7s\\cdot 3)+{3}^{2} & = \\\\ (7s+3)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our original expression factors as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(49{s}^{2}+42s+9) & = \\\\ 2(7s+3)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
